    <body>
      <div type="work" n="179">
        <pb n="226"/>
        <head>The First on the Commemoration of Bishops in General.</head>
        <head>179 — i — VI. — <quote>In the courts of the house of our God</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">Again Hymns on the Holy Fathers.</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">When we celebrate your holy memory, our sacred fathers, we receive in our mind <pb n="227"/> understanding concerning<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> the last day; on which being revealed and made known <quote>ye shall be called priests of the Lord, and <quote>ministers of our God</quote> shall be said to you</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/>. But, when you are admitted to such<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> a lot, entreat that we also may be made known among the sheep<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> on the right side; and in order that we may be admitted to enter the blissful rest, and there to praise the great mercy of <persName>Christ</persName>.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 226, n. 9</orig></choice> Ps. cxxxiv, 2.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 227, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>of</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 227, n. 2</orig></choice> Is. lxi, 3-8 <quote>And instead of..... the plantation of the Lord; and they shall increase places wasted..... from the beginning. Strangers shall rise up..... and iniquity</quote> (verbal diff.).</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 227, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>this</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 227, n. 4</orig></choice> Matth. xxv, 31-34 <quote>But, when..... that separateth the lambs from..... the kingdom which was made ready for you from the foundations of the world</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
    </body>
